# ...except the recorded reference outputs under reproduction/, which are the
# values a reader compares their own run against. The blanket *.csv above is
# scoped to data, and silently swallowed these when they were first added.
!reproduction/**/*.csv

# ...and the irrigation v3 water-system reference data (small, committed,
# checksum-pinned at load -- irrigation_v3_spec_2026-09-28.md WP1), not a
# results/audit CSV the blanket rule above is meant to catch.
!examples/irrigation_abm/data/hydrology_v3.csv
!examples/irrigation_abm/data/mead_capacity_usbr2009_1ft.csv

# ...and the WP1b Upper Basin per-sub-basin supply tables (same rationale,
# irrigation_v3_spec_2026-09-28.md item 20).
!examples/irrigation_abm/data/ub_subbasin_supply_v3.csv
!examples/irrigation_abm/data/ub_subbasin_envelope_v3.csv

# ...and the WP1b CPU-sensitivity variant supply tables (MEDIUM 4, spec 1b.6).
!examples/irrigation_abm/data/ub_subbasin_supply_v3_rho02.csv
!examples/irrigation_abm/data/ub_subbasin_supply_v3_lees_ferry_all.csv
!examples/irrigation_abm/data/ub_subbasin_supply_v3_tributary.csv
!examples/irrigation_abm/data/ub_subbasin_variant_means_v3.csv

# ...and the WP1c Lower Basin priority-split table (same rationale,
# irrigation_v3_spec_2026-09-28.md item 22).
!examples/irrigation_abm/data/lb_priority_split_v3.csv

# ...and the WP1d observed hindcast record + its sources file (same
# rationale, irrigation_v3_spec_2026-09-28.md item 25).
!examples/irrigation_abm/data/hindcast_observed_v3.csv
!examples/irrigation_abm/data/hindcast_observed_v3_sources.csv

